# PART 6 – OPERATING SYSTEM

Embedded Linux on PowerPC (and x86 for sim) runs the entire SWU stack.

| OS concept | Role in SWU |
|------------|-------------|
| **Process creation** | `ne_swumd`, `ne_swum_slave`, `alib_swus` started at boot via `ne_swum_monolite.c` |
| **Threads** | Manager uses ICN event loop; blocking waits in `AlibCs_recvData` with timeout |
| **Scheduler** | Download/install run as normal processes; long operations yield via IPC |
| **File system** | ext2/squashfs on flash; symlinks for `cur`/`next`/`prev` version switching |
| **Flash access** | Kernel MTD driver; `unpackRpm` writes through VFS; raw flash for boot sectors |
| **Memory allocation** | `Ici_malloc` for messages; `/tftpboot` on TU RAM-disk for downloads |
| **Device drivers** | Network (download), MTD/flash, EEPROM (inventory), FPGA programmers |
| **Kernel interaction** | `reboot()` syscall, `stat()`, `readlink()`, module loading on new kernel boot |
| **Signals** | Processes may handle SIGTERM on shutdown before upgrade reboot |
| **Timers** | IPC timeouts (e.g., 240s for execute command), download timeouts |
| **Logging** | `TE_TRC` → trace files; `/var/log/lumentis/swu_history.txt` |
| **Bootloader** | U-Boot or similar — reads `next` bank, loads kernel into RAM |
| **Reboot** | `doReboot()` → sync filesystems → `reboot(RB_AUTOBOOT)` → bootloader picks new image |

**Activate without immediate flash erase:** Most SWU "activation" is **symlink updates** in the filesystem — the OS and bootloader cooperate. True flash programming happens during **install/unpack**.

