# Software Downgrade: Fallback, Revert, and Rollback

In TM-3000 there is **no** `swu downgrade` command. Downgrade is handled through three different mechanisms, each for a different situation. This is a common source of confusion for new engineers.

---

## First: understand the version pointers

Every board stores software in flash, but **which version runs** is controlled by symbolic links:

```
Flash directories:
  /sw/appl/
    ├── r33a/          ← old version (still installed)
    ├── r34a/          ← new version (installed)
    ├── executing  → r34a   (what is RUNNING right now)
    ├── next       → r34a   (what will boot after reboot)
    └── previous   → r33a   (what ran before last activate)
```

| Link | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| **executing** | Software currently running in RAM |
| **next** | Software that will start after reboot |
| **previous** | Software that ran before the last activate |
| **cur** | Board-local "current" pointer (used by `doActivate`) |

**Upgrade** = install new version + move `next` to new version + reboot.

**Downgrade** = move `next` (and `cur`) back to an **older installed version** + reboot.

The old version must still be on flash. If someone ran `swu clean` or `swu delete`, downgrade may fail.

---

## Three downgrade mechanisms — when to use which

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    DOWNGRADE MECHANISMS                         │
├─────────────┬──────────────────┬────────────────────────────────┤
│  REVERT     │  FALLBACK        │  MANUAL (install + activate)   │
├─────────────┼──────────────────┼────────────────────────────────┤
│ Undo last   │ Full NE rollback │ Install older .pkg from server │
│ activation  │ to previous ENM  │ and activate if rules allow    │
├─────────────┼──────────────────┼────────────────────────────────┤
│ Per board   │ All boards       │ Per board / category           │
│ Per category│ Whole chassis    │                                │
├─────────────┼──────────────────┼────────────────────────────────┤
│ Before/after│ After failed     │ Lab testing, specific rollback │
│ reboot      │ `upgrade all all`│ needs                          │
└─────────────┴──────────────────┴────────────────────────────────┘
```

