# 1. REVERT — "Undo activation"

## What it is (simple)

You activated new software but want to **cancel** that decision. Revert sets `next` back to whatever is **currently executing** (running).

Example:
- Running: `r33a`
- You activated `r34a` → `next` = `r34a` (not rebooted yet)
- `swu revert appl all` → `next` goes back to `r33a`

**Revert does NOT:**
- Delete installed software
- Roll back an entire ENM release across all boards
- Download anything from a server

## CLI command

```shell
swu revert <cat> <slot-expr>

# Examples:
swu revert appl all          # revert application on all boards
swu revert all cu            # revert all categories on CU
swu -r revert boot 1.3       # revert + reboot slot 1.3
swu -p revert kernel tu      # prepare only (show what would happen)
swu -f revert appl all       # force (skip some checks)
```

## What happens inside the box

```
User: swu revert appl all
        ↓
mibsh_exec_sw_upgrade()
        ↓
NeSwmi_executeCommand2("revert appl all")
        ↓
ne_swum_slave → revertCommand()          [ne_swum_mgrslave_utils.c]
        ↓
For each board (Task):
    revertCommandImpl()
        ↓
    connectServer() → AlibSwui on that board
        ↓
    revertCategory() for each category
        ↓
    AlibSwui_showInstalled()  — read executing vs next
        ↓
    If next == executing → nothing to do
    If next != executing → needs revert
        ↓
    doActivateAux(swui, cat, started_version)  — activate the EXECUTING version
        ↓
    (optional) reboot with -r flag
```

## Key logic in `revertCategory()`

```863:925:git/tm3000/ne/ne_ss/ne_swum_bl/ne_swum_mgrslave_utils.c
static int
revertCategory(SelfS              *self,
               AlibSwui_Handle    swui,
               AlibSwui_CategoryE cat,
               BooleanE           doIt,
               TaskS              *task)
{
    // ...
    cfm = AlibSwui_showInstalled(swui, 0, cat, 0, NULL);

    if (cfm->next == cfm->started) { // No action — already aligned
        update = 0;
        goto clean;
    }

    // Reject if version is "only running" (not installed for next boot)
    if (cfm->data[i].status == AlibSwui_vsOnlyRunning) {
        // "Can not revert"
    }

    started = cfm->data[cfm->started].version;  // executing version

    if (doIt) {
        doActivateAux(self, swui, cat, started, task);  // next → executing
    }
    // ...
}
```

## When to use revert

| Scenario | Use revert? |
|----------|-------------|
| Activated wrong version, haven't rebooted | Yes |
| Rebooted and new SW is running | No — use **fallback** or manual install |
| Only one board wrong | Yes — `swu revert appl 1.5` |
| Whole NE upgrade failed after reboot | No — use **fallback** |

