# 4. MANUAL DOWNGRADE (install older package)

If fallback checkpoint is gone, or you need a specific older version:

```shell
# 1. Download older package
swu download ftp://server/old/osappl04a-r33a-1.powerpc.pkg

# 2. Install it
swu install appl all localhost /tftpboot/osappl04a-r33a-1.powerpc.pkg r33a

# 3. Activate it
swu -r activate appl all r33a
```

**Blocked by rules:** `checkRulesAndCapability()` may reject activation if:
- New HW requires newer SW capability
- Old SW lacks a capability required by your board revision

Example from `etc/README_swu_sw_rules.txt`:
> Prevents downgrading SW on tpQmri to 5.0 or older when HW requires 11.0+.

---

# 5. How the system knows it was a downgrade (boot reason)

After reboot, hardware layer compares versions in **PRAM** (persistent RAM):

```383:417:git/tm3000/ne/emxp2_ss/emxp2_hw_bl/emxp2_hw_bl_sysinfo.c
    if (current.versionMajor > previous.versionMajor) {
        *reason = bootReasonSwUpgrade;
    }
    else if (current.versionMajor < previous.versionMajor) {
        *reason = bootReasonSwDowngrade;
    }
    // ... minor/revision comparisons ...
    else if (current.patchLevel < previous.patchLevel) {
        *reason = bootReasonSwDowngrade;
    }
```

Board init code (`emxp2_hw_bl.c`) uses this to run downgrade-specific setup (QoS, capabilities, etc.).

